## Evidence

The history is bounded only by step count ([`engine/src/session.rs#L640-L641`](https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft/blob/00bc6a4b028013b2dfb0e85e8b326aeed3ecff6d/crates/engine/src/session.rs#L640-L641)):

```rust
/// Maximum undo depth.
const MAX_UNDO: usize = 500;
```

Each step stores `self.doc.clone()` ([`#L1003-L1020`](https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft/blob/00bc6a4b028013b2dfb0e85e8b326aeed3ecff6d/crates/engine/src/session.rs#L1003-L1020)):

```rust
self.history.push(Arc::new(Undo {
    label: label.to_string(),
    doc: self.doc.clone(),
    ...
}));
if self.history.len() > MAX_UNDO {
    self.history.remove(0);
```

Blocks are `Arc`-shared, so a small edit costs little. But a command that formats the whole document (Select All plus Bold, a style change, Clear Formatting) makes every block private. From then on, each step holds a full private copy of the document. `push_undo` follows the same rule ([`#L1023-L1030`](https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft/blob/00bc6a4b028013b2dfb0e85e8b326aeed3ecff6d/crates/engine/src/session.rs#L1023-L1030)).

Macros can run up to 10,000 steps in one call ([`engine/src/cmd/tools.rs#L825-L830`](https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft/blob/00bc6a4b028013b2dfb0e85e8b326aeed3ecff6d/crates/engine/src/cmd/tools.rs#L825-L830)), so one request can fill the whole history.

