## Evidence

`p::f32` only rejects non-finite *input* ([`engine/src/lib.rs#L150-L152`](https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft/blob/00bc6a4b028013b2dfb0e85e8b326aeed3ecff6d/crates/engine/src/lib.rs#L150-L152)), so `width: 3e38` is accepted. `place_picture` scales both sides by `width / natural width` and only then fits the width to the column ([`engine/src/cmd/insert.rs#L262-L274`](https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft/blob/00bc6a4b028013b2dfb0e85e8b326aeed3ecff6d/crates/engine/src/cmd/insert.rs#L262-L274)):

```rust
let (mut w, mut h) = (natural_w, natural_h);
if let Some(want) = width {
    let k = want.max(4.0) / w.max(1.0);
    w *= k;
    h *= k;
}
if w > max_w {
    h *= max_w / w;
    w = max_w;
}
```

For a picture taller than it is wide, `h *= k` overflows `f32` to `+inf`, and `inf * (max_w / w)` stays `inf`. The object is stored with `h = inf`.

