## Evidence

`coverage()` for format 2 ([crates/fonts/src/math.rs#L145-L166](https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft/blob/00bc6a4b028013b2dfb0e85e8b326aeed3ecff6d/crates/fonts/src/math.rs#L145-L166)):
```rust
let n = u16_at(b, at + 2).unwrap_or(0) as usize;
for i in 0..n {
    ...
    for g in s..=e {
        let k = idx as usize + (g - s) as usize;
        if k >= 70_000 {
            break;
        }
```
The `k >= 70_000` break ends only the inner loop, and only when the running index passes 70,000. Up to 65,535 range records can each cover 0..=65535 with a small start index. Every one is then walked in full: about 65,535 x 65,536 ≈ 4.3e9 iterations for one coverage table, with no work budget. A MATH table has several coverage tables (italics correction, top accent, extended shapes, vertical and horizontal variants).

`constructions()` ([#L188-L224](https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft/blob/00bc6a4b028013b2dfb0e85e8b326aeed3ecff6d/crates/fonts/src/math.rs#L188-L224)) allows up to `count` (65,535) constructions, each with up to 256 variants and 64 parts. All offsets may point at one subtable, so a small table expands to roughly 200 MB of `Construction`s held in the cached `MathTable`.

