## Evidence

In `cfb` 0.15.0, `src/lib.rs:466-507` de-duplicates the DIFAT *chain*. The FAT sector indices listed in the DIFAT are only checked against `num_sectors` before each one appends a whole sector of FAT entries (`:556-568`):

```rust
for &sector_index in difat.iter() {
    if sector_index >= num_sectors { invalid_data!(...); }
    let mut sector = sectors.seek_to_sector(sector_index)?;
    for _ in 0..(sector_len / size_of::<u32>()) {
        fat.push(sector.read_le_u32()?);
    }
}
```

The FAT is only checked for consistency (`internal/alloc.rs:119`) after it has been built. So a header whose DIFAT entries keep naming one FAT sector (4096-byte sectors) yields about 1 KB of FAT per input byte.

